sentences.l:
And of him on the spot was loosed the might, and from his hands
of great-spirited Patroclus the foot he let fall to the ground
to lie;

as indeed I have seen other men
trusting in strength and in power and in manliness
and in their own multitude, and holding a people fearless;

but they in the middle pains were suffering
from mist and war, and were worn down by pitiless bronze,
as many as were best;
